{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774721,"nonce":"4bgIRtdy5pTJuXLo+7NN1EskZLg=","title":"feat(runs): show run origin (author · trigger · ref/sha · duration) in the runs list","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #40 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/runs-list-origin` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-19T19:42:03Z · Merged: 2026-07-20T04:50:05Z\n\n\nThe repo **Runs** list was bland — a status dot, the run id shown as a fake \"sha\", and a relative time. It could not show **who** triggered a run, on **what ref/commit**, via **which trigger**, or **how long** it took. Root cause: `RunSummary` / `RunSummaryDto` were deliberately lean (id/status/created_at/tenant), and the trigger facts on the normalized `Event` were discarded after admission. (This is the gap the ADR-0054 de-mock flagged when it removed the branch/trigger/PR filters.)\n\nRequested fields: author · duration · ref sha · trigger kind · when-started · status — shown as a **grid inside each run row**, not table columns.\n\n\n- **Author is the `Actor`.** The normalized `Event` only carried an `actor` on `Manual`/`Api`; push/PR/tag/release/comment discarded the forge sender. We add a **uniform `actor`** to those variants (the pusher / PR-opener / tagger — `sender.login`, normalized) + an `Event::actor() -\u003e Option\u003c\u0026str\u003e` accessor (`None` for the internally-originated `cron`/`upstream`). New glossary term **Actor** in `CONTEXT.md` §4.5. The concept is the *actor*; the UI label reads \"author\".\n- **Actor = pusher/sender, not commit author** — \"who caused this run\", uniform across trigger kinds.\n- **Discrete columns, not a bundle.** The facts are naturally sparse (a cron run has no actor/ref/sha; only a PR has a number), so they're independently-nullable columns, mirroring how ADR-0049 stamps tenancy as two plain columns. No `RunOrigin` struct.\n- **Not \"provenance\".** That word is already SLSA/supply-chain build provenance (ADR-0015) — overloading it would collide.\n- **Live duration.** Terminal runs show the frozen `duration_ms`; in-flight runs show a ticking `now − created_at` (client-side, no backend cost).\n\n\n| Layer | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `scarab-forge` | `actor` on `Push`/`PullRequest`/`Tag`/`Release`/`Comment`; `Event::actor()` accessor |\n| adapters | GitHub + Forgejo `normalize` populate `actor` from webhook `sender` (degrades to empty, never fails) |\n| migration | `0028_run_origin.sql`: nullable `origin_trigger_kind`/`origin_actor`/`origin_ref`/`origin_sha`/`origin_pr_number` |\n| `Db` / postgres / testkit | `set_run_origin`; shared row→`RunSummary` mapper; both `list_runs*` project the columns |\n| engine / server | `RunSummary` + `RunSummaryDto` gain 5 discrete `Option` fields (via `From\u003cRunSummary\u003e`); stamped in `persist_run_from_ir` beside the tenant stamp |\n| OpenAPI / client | regenerated `openapi.json` + `schema.ts` |\n| UI | run row = grid of facts (author · ref · duration) under a header line (sha · status · trigger · when); live ticking duration; graceful per-field NULL; new `user` icon |\n\n\n- `cargo test --workspace` green (Postgres-gated integration tests skip locally).\n- New `Event::actor()` contract test (principal events, cron→None, empty→None).\n- Strengthened both adapters' normalize tests to assert `sender` → actor.\n- UI `npm run build` (tsc + vite) green.\n- Postgres-backed origin round-trip (stamp → `list_runs` projection) is exercised by the existing trigger/list integration tests once run against a real DB — worth a live check via the `just` stack before merge.\n\n\n_Not captured in this session — the row renders author · ref · live-ticking duration under a sha · status · trigger · when header. Happy to attach one from `just ui` on request._\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}